ny people making demands on my time  many of which you know are paying me for  for that and I have to do a good job  with all of my clients with the people  who I consult with with my students with  everybody else and I do do some pro bono  work right in a very few cases with with  clients you know where I think that that  it's really deserved or sometimes with  institutions I get free talks at  libraries and give about you know 30 a  year or so but when you know for the  most part the stuff that I do I actually  have to be compensated for it because I  do so much pro bono stuff I put out on  average now about two hundred and fifty  videos per year of new content I respond  to a lot of comments and I devote you  know a good portion of each day I would  say I probably devote between shooting  videos planning videos responding to  comments I probably devote anywhere the  average day from two to four hours to  that and that's you know that's a lot of  time so you know when you're thinking  about why isn't dr. Sadler willing to  engage on this particular topic with me  a you know a lot of it is a factor of  time and time well-spent you know I also  have to have enough time to work out to  live a healthy life to to devote to my  my wife and my children and my pets and  my family you know spread out in other  places and my friends and my community  all of that is is important so all of  that puts things into perspective I  think another thing that I'd like to say  as well is that you know I think that a  lot of people have this expectation  that if you're putting your content  there on YouTube somehow you made some  sort of contract with the viewer and if  they say something you have to respond  to them that's total BS if you know to  begin with comments I don't even have to  leave them on my channel if I want to  delete every single comment that people  put which I'm never gonna do that would  be perfectly within my rights as a not  only legal but moral rights as a Content  producer my channel is sort of like my  front porch and so if you're coming onto  my front porch and dr. Sattler dish you  know I'm wanting to argue with me I'll  kick you off my front porch because I  don't want you there oh if you have bad  things to say insert so you're swearing  at me I'm not gonna deal with you right  I'll just you know block you and delete  your comment because it's not it's not  worth it  I mean if you if you if you feel that I  owe to you to engage in debate when I'm  providing high quality video content for  free and I have been for what six years  now there's a kind of skewed perspective  going at and and where does this  perspective come from I think that the  biggest place other than a sense of  entitlement that that a lot of people  have is this metaphor that we we throw  around we talk about the marketplace of  ideas right and it's sort of like well  anybody who puts their idea out there  has to defend it has to be prepared to  defend it to the teeth no they don't  that's not the way the world works it's  only a metaphor and you know we don't  all have to defend everything all the  time as a matter of fact it's often  enough just to put the things out there  and and we've already made a major  contribution to whatever marketplace of  ideas you want to talk about and the  other thing to keep in mind is you know  if you if you view yourself as you know  a skeptic or a critic or somebody who's  doing yeoman's work in the marketplace  of ideas you better really know your  stuff right or else your  wasting again wasting everybody else's  time the marketplace of ideas works best  when we have exchanges between people  who really do understand the material  and have legitimate differences that can  then be brought to light it's not about  you know answering the same questions  over and over and over and over again at  the same basic level another thing to  keep in mind I think that that's quite  important is you know I know that  there's a lot of people who you know  shoot YouTube videos and they don't  really know what they're talking about  when it comes to philosophy I know that  because I I see their videos and  occasionally very very very occasionally  I'll comment and say well this is I  think they've got so-and-so wrong or I  think this this is not actually what  Aristotle is saying I'm not that way if  if I put something out there it's it's  because I've put in some time and done  some research some of the thinkers who  I'm presenting on I've been reading  since my teens or 20s and I've been  studying in a serious way for years and  years I've been teaching philosophy for  decades I've made solid contributions to  the field in terms of scholarship and in  terms of popular work you know if I if I  tell you that Nietzsche says X or that  that you know Hegel says X or Kant says  X probably they actually do there are  legitimate differences in interpretation  between scholars and and and experts but  you know those are usually carried out  in a sort of that well sometimes not but  usually kept a civil and respectful way  in which both both parties or multiple  parties acknowledge the expertise of the  other person so you know odds are if you  hear me saying something about Aristotle  and you don't think it's right and it  doesn't quite jibe with what you  read in this history of philosophy or  remember from your you know your class  that you took or what your favorite  professor said probably I actually know  what I'm talking about and there are  cases where I'm you know I'm wrong and  I'll admit it but that's not usually  going to come up through YouTube  comments  I do mispronounce things I do when I'm  writing things on the board misspelled  that's that's life right but that's  pretty pretty pretty small stuff and  that's and that's not even worth  debating about right so I'm a bad  speller the content is what matters so  you know the the last thing that I'm  gonna say about about debates because  you know before that here's here's the  other thing about time right if you're  trying to get me you know trying to show  me that I've got something wrong that's  probably not a good use of your time  because you may in fact you know hit the  bull's eye that one time but but most of  the time you're actually gonna have been  barking up the wrong tree  so the last thing that I'm gonna say  about debates is that you know when I  was an undergraduate and even a graduate  student I really did enjoy the agonistic  experience of getting in there and  scrapping and on all of that and I spent  a good portion of my life trying to get  past that I don't think that's a  particularly useful model for doing  philosophy well I understand that in  some schools they kind of teach that as  the the mo right and it does you know  appeal to certain kinds of people but  that's not how advances in philosophy  for the most part take place and it  doesn't matter whether you're talking  about you know Nietzsche  or you know Aristotle or Ansem or  whoever the temperament of the  philosopher doesn't necessarily dictate  the way in which we should go about  talking about them or debating about  them  so I tend to avoid debates if somebody  really wants to try to push it with me  you know my suggestion is book me for a  tutorial session and I'll be happy to do  that with you if it if it comes down to  the need for my debating some other  public figure on some topic my question  is gonna be a camp can't somebody else  do that there's so many other people out  there who love doing that sort of  activity and I would prefer to like you  know put stuff on the blackboard and get  stuff done with the time yeah but you  know if need be and I have to debate  somebody I suppose I will if it's for  the public good but if it's something  that you just want because you you know  you think that this is a way to improve  your understanding of of you know mock  Schaller or you know Jacques Lacan or  whoever yeah book my time you know show  me that it really is valuable to you and  I'll take you just as seriously as I do  my many other clients who book my time  because they think that it's it's worth  doing but if you don't want to do that  and then don't be surprised if when I  think you're trying to get me involved  in a debate I put this video oh because  frankly it's it's you know this is a  great time-saver for for me so that's  all I really have to say about this  topic
 

